NiteLite for the Series 3c (backlit version)
Written by Andrew Moore
Version 1.00

*******************************************************************************

Brief:
NiteLite is a simple program which automatically switches on the backlight
when the Series 3c is switched on during a set period. Typical use would
be using the Series 3c as a bedside clock.

*******************************************************************************

To install:
Copy the NITELITE.IMG file to an \IMG\ directory on your Series 3c.

To use:
Select NiteLite from under the Run Img icon. When NiteLite is first run
you are presented with the setup dialog. The options are:

Start time:	The time from which you want NiteLite to come active.
End time: 	The time when NiteLite deactivates itself.
Duration:	The time in seconds before NiteLite switches off (when active).
Clock:		If set to yes, NiteLite displays a large clock when active.

To quit:
Press System. Highlight NiteLite under the Run Img icon. Press Delete to kill
the application.

To reset preferences:
Quit NiteLite, then re-run.


